  "interpretations": {
    "G6.liveness": "liveness is judged per session over the runner's launch and process-exit stamps with power_telemetry.energy_between_uj (the analysis's own function: too few samples, a stamp outside the sampled range or a sample flagged decrease or gap = no session energy), plus no backwards step, no gap over 30 s, the counter advancing and never flat over 5 s; the sampler's invocation-wide verdicts are information only",
    "G6.incomplete_session": "a session whose schedule status is not complete (a coverage outcome or a failure) is judged by G1/A1, not G6: G6 is not_applicable for it",
    "G7.scope": "applied to the gpu.csv trapezoid cross-check (measured windows and idle windows >= 10 s); the RAPL series are judged by G6 (flags, liveness), not G7",
    "G7.gap": "a gap is the spacing of consecutive samples whose interval overlaps the window, boundary intervals included",
    "G8.clean_onset": "an onset is usable only if gpu.csv shows the GPU quiet (utilization.gpu < 10% in every sample) just before the reference stamp (the window start or the pulse's launch stamp). A window: quiet over the 1.0 s before the stamp, then the onset is the first sample >= 10% in [stamp, stamp + 3 s] (windows follow each other and the query's warm-up run within milliseconds: activity in the last second is earlier work, not the window's onset). A pulse: quiet over [stamp - 2 s, stamp - 1 s), then the onset is the first sample >= 10% in [stamp - 1 s, stamp + 3 s] and the lag is signed, so a stream stamped ahead of the worker's clock (a negative lag) is scored and fails the +-0.4 s rule (the runner waits for a quiet GPU before every pulse). A window or pulse with a sample >= 10% in its quiet range (busy_before) or no sample there (quiet_not_shown) has no onset: counted in the QA table (windows_skipped, pulses_skipped), never scored as a lag. With fewer than two usable window onsets a session falls back to its load pulses (implementation clarification of section 4 G8, amendment A3, made before any study data)",
    "G8.drift": "first-third versus last-third = median lag of the first max(1, n // 3) usable onsets minus that of the last max(1, n // 3); needs n >= 2 (the probe tool reports no drift below six onsets and passes; the gate evaluates it)",
    "G8.chrony": "the design says the offset is logged, with no threshold: a missing log fails G8, a logged one never does",
    "G8.not_evaluable": "a session with fewer than two onsets from its windows and its pulses together is not_evaluable: counted in the QA table, its gpu.csv values are disabled like a failed session's, and it is never a pass",
    "G9.median_trial": "the median trial of a query is the one with the median per-run time of its trials",
    "G9.window_rule": "a window that does not follow the stop rule (n < 50 needs sum of the first n-1 runs < target <= sum of all n) is a rule violation, reported as its own reason; the cell is not usable",
    "G10.difference": "relative difference = |post - pre| / mean(pre, post), the pair difference of the P5 probe",
    "G10.scopes": "the GPU counter, and on a RAPL host S2-all (power_telemetry.all_package_dram_zones; every series for a source that is not per socket) and S2-pinned (power_telemetry.pinned_energy_zones) where attribution is possible, each summed by power_telemetry.s2_pinned_energy_j; a scope that exists on the host but has no valid energy in both idle windows (for instance a window that touches a flagged sample) makes the session's above-idle unreliable",
    "G11.logged": "G11 passes when the throttle reasons, the temperature and the power-limit text are logged for the session; throttling actually observed is reported as a count, not judged",
    "G12.scheduled": "'nothing else scheduled' is judged against an explicit allow-list in the host config (cron, at, systemd timers captured at the start and end of the round)"
  },
